## Cybercrimes laws

Cybercrime laws are rules made to stop illegal activities using computers or digital tools. They explain what cybercrimes are and set punishments for those who commit them. They also guide police on how to catch and punish cybercriminals. Cybercrimes include hacking, identity theft, fraud, data breaches, cyberbullying, online harassment, stealing intellectual property, and cyber terrorism. Examples are breaking into computer systems, phishing scams, malware
